FFmpeg
------
Copyright (c) the FFmpeg developers
Source: https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg

WasFlash uses the following FFmpeg libraries, built from source:
  libavformat, libavcodec, libavutil, libswscale, libswresample

FFmpeg is built with the following flags (no GPL components enabled):
  --disable-shared --enable-static --disable-programs --disable-doc
  --disable-network

Most files in FFmpeg are licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public
License version 2.1 or later (LGPL v2.1+). Some files within FFmpeg carry
MIT, X11, or BSD-style licenses; in combination, LGPL v2.1+ applies to
FFmpeg as a whole. WasFlash does not pass --enable-gpl, --enable-version3,
or --enable-nonfree, so no GPL components are active.

See the LGPL Relinking Notice above for how object files are distributed
to satisfy the static linking requirement.

FFmpeg source code and full license details are available at:
https://ffmpeg.org/download.html

